  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A circle is inscribed in an equilateral triangle, and a square is inscribed in the circle. The ratio of the area of the triangle to the area of the square is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt3:1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt3:\\sqrt2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(3\\sqrt3:2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(3:\\sqrt2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(3:2\\sqrt2\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1963-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If the circle has radius \\(r,\\) the equilateral triangle has side \\(2\\sqrt3r\\) and area \\(3\\sqrt3r^2.\\) The square has side \\(r\\sqrt2\\) and area \\(2r^2.\\) The ratio is \\(3\\sqrt3:2.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Express both areas using the circle’s radius \\(r\\)",
        "The triangle’s side is \\(2\\sqrt3r\\) and the square’s diagonal is \\(2r\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
